ASSISTANT: Got it — I'll build an hourly automation that reads your Orders table, loops through each order, and sends a confirmation email to each customer. Before I start, I need to check your connections.

First, let me look at your Orders table and find your email integration.
TOOL_CALL: ap_select_project {"projectId":"eval-project"}
TOOL_RESULT: null
TOOL_CALL: ap_list_across_projects {"title":"Check connections","activeTitle":"Checking your connected apps","doneTitle":"Checked your connected apps","resource":"connections"}
TOOL_RESULT: null
ASSISTANT: Let me get a connection set up for your email. Which email app should I use to send the confirmation emails?
TOOL_CALL: ap_show_connection_picker {"piece":"gmail","displayName":"Gmail"}
TOOL_RESULT: {"dismissed":true,"message":"The user chose not to select a Gmail account. Do not pick one on their behalf. Ask: \"Would you like me to continue building with a placeholder you can connect later, or would you prefer to stop here?\""}
ASSISTANT: No worries! To send confirmation emails, I'll need to know which email app you'd like to use. What do you have available?
TOOL_CALL: ap_show_questions {"questions":[{"type":"choice","question":"Which email app should I use to send the confirmation emails?","options":[{"label":"Gmail","piece":"gmail"},{"label":"Outlook","piece":"microsoft-outlook"},{"label":"SMTP","icon":"mail"},{"label":"Other","icon":"mail"}]}]}
TOOL_RESULT: {"dismissed":true,"message":"The user skipped these questions. Proceed with reasonable defaults where possible, and let the user know what assumptions you made."}
ASSISTANT: I'll go ahead and build this with Gmail as the default email sender — you can swap it out for any other email app later. Let me also need a Gmail connection to actually send the emails. Let me get that set up.
